4. Constant Baseline MODE_V ((V) Vector-Table Addressing)

• In Z80_EXTEND, MODE_V is permanently active on the Main Page.
• Every (nn) and (HL) memory slot on the Main Page fetches 1 immediate byte V, forms (IXH << 8) + V, reads a 16-bit real target address from memory, and executes against that target (when PACKED_MODE == 1 && IXH == 0x00, vector resolution targets local SRAM directly).
• Direct non-(V) memory access ((HL+d), (RR+d), LD RR,(nn), LD (nn),RR, JP (RR)) is covered by the 7 RR pages and Super-CB.

5. Unified Replay, Repeater & Predication Engine

• Instruction-Replay Latch: CPU latches START_PC[15:0] (or START_SRAM_PC[15:0]), TARGET_OP[7:0], and PREFIX_STATE on Iteration 1; Iterations 2..N replay directly from the latch without M1 fetches (INT/NMI pushes START_PC for seamless resume).
• R0–R7 (0x98–0x9F, 1001 1xxx): 6-bit shift-accumulating counter (STAGE1 << 3) | STAGE2 (0..63 repeats). Anti-dumb guard: Any instruction fetching immediate bytes (n, nn, d, V) automatically nullifies REP_CNT = 0.
• Constructive Block Primitives (On all RR Pages):
	• INCINC (0xC0) / DECDEC (0xD0): Post-increment / post-decrement active pointer(s) (RR, and DE on 2-pointer ops).
	• REPBC (0xE0): Repeat while BC != 0 (BC--).
	• REPNZ (0xF0): Repeat while BC != 0 AND Z == 0 (BC--).
	• REPB (0xC8): Repeat while B != 0 (B--).
• ACT_CC Predication (0x88–0x8F, 1000 1ccc): Conditionally executes the following instruction (NZ, Z, NC, C, PO, PE, P, M), suppressing write-backs if false without branching.
• CARRY Prefix (0xDD on Main Page): Arms Carry/Borrow for the next ADD/SUB (8-bit or 16-bit).

